    "recommendations": "Providing address numbers that are clearly visible from the street and from the access road could significantly improve responder navigation on approach, particularly given the length of the driveway and single entry point. Marking or identifying the primary access point at the street frontage may assist responding units in locating the correct entry without delay. The circular driveway configuration would support apparatus turnaround and staging, and keeping that area clear of parked vehicles or temporary obstructions could enhance operational efficiency upon arrival. Coordinating with responders in advance regarding the limited rear access may help inform tactical planning, as dense vegetation along the perimeter could reduce visibility and movement options for personnel working around the structure."
