    "recommendations": "Reducing the continuity of scattered shrub vegetation across the property could meaningfully lower the opportunity for fire to spread toward the structure, and creating or widening spacing between individual shrubs and any shrub groupings near the building perimeter would support defensible space improvement. Vegetation growing in direct proximity to the structure should be managed to increase separation between combustible fuels and exterior surfaces, and the tree cluster on the property would benefit from limbing and clearing of any surface vegetation beneath the canopy to reduce vertical fuel connections. The long single-access driveway should be kept clear of overhanging vegetation along its full length to support firefighter entry and occupant evacuation. Maintaining the irrigated landscaping in its current condition provides a valuable low-fuel buffer near the structure and should be preserved. Where open terrain exists around the property, retaining that natural fuel break could further reduce fuel continuity and support suppression operations."
